es, or independently grounded confidence in providence. Live burden: The defender must supply more than human ignorance to make divine care reasonable, while Grayling must address whether antecedent evidence for God could legitimately alter the evidential significance of otherwise inscrutable harms. Locked score: This coherent, centrally relevant, and charitable reply decisively contacts epistemic restraint and recompense, yet its incomplete treatment of broader unknown-reason strategies keeps evidential warrant below its strongest dimensions and supports the locked very-strong score of 88."}]}
